// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6264 New Rule: Potential Indirect Command Execution Via XBootMgr.EXE
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6264
// Pull request author: COMPUMAX-EC
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Indirect Command Execution Via XBootMgr.EXE
// Sigma ID: 446e9bb7-804d-4dfe-9a9f-576d9ce35a3b
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Geovanny Basantes
// Date: 2026-08-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects execution of "xbootmgr.exe" (Windows Performance Toolkit boot/trace tool) with the
//   "-callBack" or "-preTraceCmd" arguments, which cause it to launch an arbitrary executable before
//   or after a performance trace completes. This can be abused as a way to execute a payload through
//   a legitimate, signed Microsoft binary.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate performance-trace automation scripts that use the "-callBack" or "-preTraceCmd" parameters
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/9c5e3841081cac342e7603093253cb51512c8369/yml/OtherMSBinaries/XBootMgr.yml
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e33996585f73029bfeb4499d2c8f625af12343b8/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_xbootmgr_indirect_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\xbootmgr.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "xbootmgr.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-callBack" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-preTraceCmd")
